  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. I haven't tested the fix against a real nested-group case.\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py:392`), a child context copied the parent's whole `default_map`. A subcommand then looked up its parameters at the top level instead of under its own name. For example, `{\"sub\": {\"opt\": 1}}` was searched for `opt` and never found.\n\n**Fix:** the child context now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, so the subcommand's own section is used.\n\n**Tests:** the existing suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). It has no test for this case, so I didn't add one and nothing is committed.\n\nIf the parent map has no entry for the subcommand, the child's `default_map` is `None`. That matches Click's documented behavior for nested `default_map` entries.",
